KG42.register("clusters-5edbc6c00e7c6bfdbbdc4285",{"id":"09-local_flexibility::v142-d-CL001","paper":"09-local_flexibility","label":"Procurement clearing and conditional payments for mutually exclusive service requests","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-CL001","label":"Procurement clearing and conditional payments for mutually exclusive service requests","market_meaning":"The market makes an economic selection from the DSO's list of mutually exclusive requests; when the purchased service is conditional, the activation fee determined by clearing is linked to the DSO's obligations to make standby and activation payments to aggregators. The current chains can form a candidate assembly of procurement and its fee consequences, but they cannot yet constitute a complete executable clearing and settlement rule.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["DEM","LEM"],"process_stages":["clearing","pricing","settlement"],"scope_disposition":"unresolved","scope_explanation":"All citations refer to the M01 procurement market of EcoGrid 2.0, and R004 and R005 apply only to the conditional branch of the services purchased under R001. The classification relationship between DEM in R001 and LEM in the other two chains has not been explained; both labels are retained and the unresolved classification is recorded, without extending conditional payments to scheduled services.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"The selection result defines the procurement objects, the clearing result of the same market determines the activation fees for conditional services, and the payment chain further specifies the paying entity and the obligations corresponding to activation states; the three chains therefore have direct decision and fee linkages. Locational eligibility and request-publication governance each have independent conditions and obligations and form separate clusters.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R001","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provides mutually exclusive request selection and procurement results, constituting the transaction entry point to which the subsequent conditional fee arrangements apply; retains its existing mathematical expressions and unresolved interpretations."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R004","ownership":"primary","role":"interface","rationale":"Connects procurement clearing to the formation of activation fees for conditional services; it overlaps with the fee-determination statement in R005 and is not counted as another independent payment rule."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R005","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Specifies the DSO's two-part payments to aggregators and the non-activated and activated branches, presenting fee formation together with payment obligations."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-CN001","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R001::V::clearing.local","v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-X001","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R004::V::clearing.local","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E12","v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g02-e26"],"rationale":"The source places procurement clearing for mutually exclusive requests and the fee arrangements for purchased conditional services within the same market: the final activation cost is determined by the clearing result. This mapping links the two chains only when the purchased service is conditional, without interpreting the procurement-selection indicator as an activation indicator or presuming a specific pricing algorithm."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CN002","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R004::V::pricing.local","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R005::V::settlement.payment","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C001","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C002","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C003","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e26","v141-b-g01-E02"],"rationale":"The same source paragraph states that the activation cost in aggregator bids is determined by clearing and that the DSO bears the activation fee; the payment source additionally specifies the standby and activation components and the branch in which only the standby price is paid when activation does not occur. The two chains express fee formation and payment obligations separately; only an assembly linkage is established here, without adding a C scientific edge from pricing to settlement."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-OM001","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::V::clearing.local","v141-c-R004::V::clearing.local","v141-c-R005::V::clearing.local"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E12","v141-b-g02-e26"],"rationale":"Request selection and conditional activation fees in the source both belong to the clearing function of the same M01 market, supporting identity correspondence among the three existing node references. The different local uses concerning selection, fee formation, and payment linkage in the respective chains are retained; node correspondence does not eliminate differences in market-type labels or merge their constraints or edges."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-OM002","kind":"alternative_representation","member_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C001"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e26"],"rationale":"Both items concern the determination of the activation amount for conditional services by clearing, emphasizing cost formation and payable fees respectively, and are retained as alternative statements of overlapping matters. The source does not provide definitions of amount objects or allocation among aggregators, so the expressions are not yet declared fully identical, nor are the existing edges with two different endpoints treated as the same edge."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-G001","category":"math_incomplete","description":"R001 translates economic selection into maximizing B_s alone, but the cited passage explicitly establishes only the DSO benefit and willingness to pay represented by B_s and does not demonstrate that it is the complete clearing objective incorporating bids and feasibility. The existing selection expression requires one item to be selected when the list is nonempty, whereas the mutual-exclusivity expression alone merely restricts multiple selections; the treatment of empty lists, the absence of feasible bids, and tied benefits is unspecified.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-T001","v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-X001","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C001","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E11","v141-b-g01-E12","v141-b-g01-E14","v141-b-g02-e27"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g02-prop-dso-willingness-to-pay","v141-b-g02-prop-service-request-selection"],"required_work":"Have the upstream layer supply the relevant algorithmic basis from [61], as referenced by the source, and review the economic objective, the role of bids, conditions for concluding trades, and tie handling; if the source remains insufficient, retain the unresolved status and address it in a subsequent version of C without rewriting the expressions frozen in this round."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G002","category":"math_incomplete","description":"R004 and R005 provide only fee determination and payment branches, lacking calculations, units, and allocation definitions for the standby price and final activation fee. The overlapping statements of cost and payable fees do not support inferring a uniform clearing unit price, pay-as-bid payment, or equal amounts for each aggregator, nor can B_s substitute for the activation fee.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R004","v141-c-R005"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C001","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C002","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C003","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E02","v141-b-g02-e26","v141-b-g02-e27"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Supply the basis for pricing, standby fees, and payment amounts in M01, and check the measurement levels of costs and fees; until that basis is obtained, maintain the procedural statements and linked_distinct mapping, without borrowing M02 valuation formulas to fill gaps in settlement."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G003","category":"upstream_missing","description":"R001 allows multiple aggregators to jointly deliver the same purchased service, but the existing chains contain no aggregator-award, delivery-share, or standard-contract objects; the request-selection result therefore cannot yet be connected item by item to payment obligations for each aggregator.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R005"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C002","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C001","v141-c-R005::V::settlement.payment"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E12","v141-b-g02-e26"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g01-prop-aggregator","v141-b-g02-prop-aggregator-participation"],"required_work":"The upstream layer should supply source support for allocation among multiple aggregators and for contract and payment objects, and establish referenceable interfaces in a subsequent version of C; maintain the unapproved status of the aggregator proposal."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G004","category":"upstream_missing","description":"The payment branches depend on whether purchased conditional services are activated, but the five chains supplied in this round do not include DSO activation-decision and signal chains. In R001, y_s represents procurement selection and cannot also serve as the activation state; the current assembly can treat the activation state only as an externally given condition.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R005"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-X001","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C003","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g02-e26"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g02-prop-conditional-activation","v141-b-g03-prop-02"],"required_work":"Based on M01, add an independent chain for activation conditions, responsible entities, and signal interfaces, and check the mechanism scope of the relevant proposals awaiting review; before this is done, do not incorporate M02 scenario activation assumptions or indicators into procurement variables."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G005","category":"scope_conflict","description":"R001 is labeled DEM, while R004 and R005 are labeled LEM. Although the source narratives refer to the same EcoGrid 2.0 procurement process, the input provides no basis for correspondence between the two market classifications.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R004","v141-c-R005"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::V::clearing.local","v141-c-R004::V::clearing.local","v141-c-R005::V::clearing.local"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E12","v141-b-g02-e26"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Have the upstream layer check the market-type coding and applicable definitions; retain the union of DEM and LEM in this round, without using functional identity correspondence to eliminate classification differences."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G006","category":"ontology_extension","description":"Service-request selection, flexibility products, and the standby and activation payment structure currently use generic clearing, pricing, and payment nodes, and all related refinement proposals remain unapproved. The boundaries and object interpretations of this cluster do not constitute approval of ontology extensions.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R004","v141-c-R005"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::V::clearing.local","v141-c-R004::V::pricing.local","v141-c-R005::V::settlement.payment"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E01","v141-b-g01-E02","v141-b-g01-E12"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g01-prop-flex-service","v141-b-g02-prop-flexibility-service-product","v141-b-g02-prop-service-request-selection","v141-b-g01-prop-reserve-activation-payment","v141-b-g02-prop-reserve-activation-payment"],"required_work":"Manually examine the overlap and necessity of the proposals before deciding whether to refine their representation in subsequent ontology and C versions; do not directly equate flexibility services with local energy products or add new nodes."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G007","category":"unverified_source","description":"The B evidence used in this cluster currently remains unverified and is used for assembly solely because of its experimental candidate eligibility; the B source-text audit, independent C2 review, and work by Agent E have not been performed, and the mathematics and mappings have no independent scientific acceptance.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R004","v141-c-R005"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C001","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E01","v141-b-g01-E02","v141-b-g01-E11","v141-b-g01-E12","v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g01-E14","v141-b-g02-e26","v141-b-g02-e27"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Subsequently, conduct manual examination cluster by cluster and chain by chain, checking the corresponding original texts, conditions, and transcriptions; maintain the original source_status and candidate nature until the review is complete."}]},"rule_refs":["09-local_flexibility::v141-c-R001","09-local_flexibility::v141-c-R004","09-local_flexibility::v141-c-R005"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-459c6c859f38f049","COMP-60443ad093294c09","COMP-71b68181dcd38d38"]});
